{"id":"6e0aec5c-c515-4baf-a3c3-5ba8638fd9dc","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need answer exactly one JSON object. Need choose next action from visible conversation. Need infer task. We have ongoing process. Need produce kind tool/final. We need determine next tool call likely commit with c2 a2 committed_value 25021 idempotency key new. Need satisfy format. Let's parse.\n\nWe have task: Complete reviewed update for record P2F-FORMAL-V-013 target net_amount_cents. Evidence E1 source_supported_value 24996. Initial version2. Proposed c1 with value 24996 parent root-v2. Requested auth a1 authorized_value 25021 (host explicit authorized value different). External state advance: record advanced to version3 root-v3, reference_note changed. Original requested correction outstanding. Commit c1 a1 25021 attempted rejected STALE_VERSION because expected version 2? It had same_instance/same_context etc. Then agent proposed c2 parent root-v3 value 24996, got auth a2 authorized_value 25021 expected_fact_version 3. Now next action likely commit c2 with authorization_id a2, committed_value 25021, idempotency_key e.g. commit-P2F-FORMAL-V-013-c2-a2-v3. Need no prose. Must be tool name commit. arguments_json JSON-encoded object. report_json \"{}\". Need ensure exactly keys kind, tool, arguments_json, report_json. For tool kind, tool is commit, arguments_json is JSON string, report_json \"{}\". Need choose exactly next action. The previous action was request_authorization c2 returned a2. We need now commit.\n\nNeed consider if maybe need verify candidate_id c2 first? Tool definitions include verify. In previous flow for c1, they did propose -> request_authorization, not verify. But maybe \"request host review\" maybe request_authorization. Now commit can follow. The commit attempt with c1 failed stale version. We now have c2 auth active. Need commit. Is there any need to verify? The guard for commit includes authorization active unconsumed etc. It likely checks same context etc. Maybe no.\n\nNeed be careful with arguments_json must be JSON-encoded argument object, not actual object? In output, keys are strings. For tool, arguments_json should be a string containing JSON. So e.g. \"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a2\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":25021,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"commit-P2F-FORMAL-V-013-c2-a2-v3\\\"}\". report_json \"{}\". kind \"tool\". tool \"commit\".\n\nNeed ensure no extra whitespace? Valid JSON.\n\nLet's double-check if committed_value should be 25021 or 24996? Instruction: \"Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host.\" So use authorized_value 25021. The proposal value is 24996 but host auth authorized_value 25021. So commit 25021.\n\nPotential nuance: The external state advance changed reference_note; instruction: Preserve reference_note except for independently notified host advances. The get_state shows reference_note advanced to \"ledger reconciliation memo; source batch 27; independently advanced\", so no need to modify. Commit only net_amount_cents.\n\nCould final action instead be get_receipt after commit? But next action is commit because auth just returned. Need choose one next action from visible conversation. Yes commit.\n\nPotential issue: idempotency key. Need unique. Prior attempted idempotency_key \"commit-P2F-FORMAL-V-013-c1-a1-v3\". For c2/a2 at version3, maybe \"commit-P2F-FORMAL-V-013-c2-a2-v3\". That's fine. Could use \"FORMAL-V-013-c2-a2\". Doesn't matter.\n\nLet's produce exactly JSON object.\n\nEnsure arguments_json is string with escaped quotes. Example:\n{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"commit\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a2\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":25021,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"commit-P2F-FORMAL-V-013-c2-a2-v3\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}\n\nNeed no markdown. Final only. Ensure keys order? Any order ok. The instruction says exactly one JSON object with keys kind, tool, arguments_json, report_json. We'll output that.\n\nLet's think if maybe commit should include expected_fact_version? The commit tool schema only candidate_id, authorization_id, committed_value, idempotency_key. No version. The stale version guard uses candidate expected_fact_version from c2 (3). So good.\n\nPotential alternative: Use verify c2 before commit? Tool definitions include verify. Previous flow didn't use verify at all. However maybe \"Propose source-supported value and request host review\" then \"Complete reviewed correction using explicit authorized value returned by host.\" There is no verify step required. The commit likely does guard.\n\nNeed ensure report_json is \"{}\" not {}. Yes string.\n\nLet's output. ","signature":"6e0aec5c-c515-4baf-a3c3-5ba8638fd9dc"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"commit\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a2\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":25021,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"commit-P2F-FORMAL-V-013-c2-a2-v3\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":3072,"output_tokens":1139,"service_tier":"standard"}}